ited files (e.g. a scoped denylist of live-alias assertions such as 'is a permanent alias'/'still honored'/'alias:' outside explicitly-marked history sections), so the check is both falsifiable and does not flag the intended ADR 0116 migration text.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.0975,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["docs/release-notes.md:730-732 and 756-759 already carry historical 'still honored' statements naming six of the renames; the plan itself commits to CORRECTING these as historical release notes rather than deleting the old spellings","docs/config.md lines 854-862 name all eight spellings in Back-compat prose that becomes migration/history text","the plan's own Approach says remaining occurrences are classified as 'intentional tests, ADR/history, or migration documentation' — a semantic distinction the described 'machine-checkable' census cannot make on string presence alone","the eight retired spellings must APPEAR in the new changelog/migration mapping by design, so a naive presence check would flag the intended content"],"finding":"The RED-first census oracle's discrimination mechanism is under-specified: it must fail on 'live-alias guidance' but PASS on the historical/migration references the plan deliberately adds to the same files (docs/config.md, docs/release-notes.md) and the ADR. A plain string-presence census over the eight spellings cannot mechanically separate a forbidden live-alias claim from a permitted historical/migration mention, so as written the oracle is either unfalsifiable (allowlists whole files) or over-broad (flags the intended migration docs).","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fb076d7e5634ff63f","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Testing — 'RED-first documentation oracle: a complete-population census/check that fails while live-alias guidance remains'; Approach — 'classify remaining occurrences as intentional tests, ADR/history, or migration documentation'","norm_i